-- ============================================================
-- Marksmanship: Rapid Killing
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Rank 1 reduces Rapid Fire's cooldown by 1.5 min and Rank 2 by
--  3 min, and your Steady Shot, Arcane Shot, Chimera Shot and Aimed Shot reset
--  the duration of Pack Hunting.  (2 ranks)"
--
-- The cooldown half is one column.  Base points -90001 / -180001 render as
-- 1.5 / 3 through $/60000;s2, since a flat modifier's value is
-- BasePoints + max(1, DieSides).  Retail was -1 / -2 min; this is the rank
-- split restored after a briefly-shipped flat -2 min on both ranks left rank 2
-- doing nothing at all.
--
-- The existing mask (EffectSpellClassMaskB1 = 32, Rapid Fire) and MiscValue 11
-- (SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN) are already right.  Rapid Fire has RecoveryTime 0 and a
-- 300s CategoryRecoveryTime, which the modifier does reach --
-- Player::AddSpellAndCategoryCooldowns applies SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN to catrec too,
-- gated only on SPELL_ATTR6_NO_CATEGORY_COOLDOWN_MODS, which 3045 lacks.
--
-- The second half REPLACES an earlier design in which a killing blow reset Pack
-- Hunting's cooldown and buffed pet threat for 30s.  A cooldown reset on kill
-- is worth little in practice -- it lands when the pull is already over.
-- Refreshing the DURATION instead makes Pack Hunting something the rotation
-- sustains: keep shooting and the threat redirect stays up, stop and it falls
-- off after its 10s.
--
-- Refreshing a duration is not something the DBC can express.  There is no
-- "refresh aura" spell effect in 3.3.5, and a triggered re-cast of Pack Hunting
-- would re-run SPELL_EFFECT_REDIRECT_THREAT and re-register the redirect, as
-- well as burning the 20s cooldown.  Aura::RefreshDuration (SpellAuras.cpp:822)
-- is what is actually wanted, so Effect1 is a plain dummy and
-- spell_hun_rapid_killing does the refresh.
--
-- Effect1 is a dummy rather than a PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL pointing at 0: the script
-- prevents the default action either way, but a proc-trigger effect with no
-- trigger spell is a lie in the data.



